comments.body:
Published a fix in my fork: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/4fb09e6b (branch [`fix/issue-batch-1023pm`](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/issue-batch-1023pm), based on current main).

Your diagnosis was exact — both allowance readers dropped a `Windows: []` reading whole, balance or not:

- live: `Allowances`' reader goroutine (`internal/provider/routing.go`), the `len(q.Windows) == 0` continue you quoted;
- on-disk fallback: `lastAllowances` (`internal/provider/quota_last.go`) had the same `len(q.Windows) > 0` guard, so a restart flipped the account back to not-known until a fresh reading came in.

Both now take a successful reading with no windows but a balance as **known, with an empty allowance** — there is genuinely no window that stops the account: the balance is the Usage page's meter, and the vendor's own insufficient-balance answer rests the account (as #3289's 402 handling does). Routing weighs it as known and unused; the Routing page no longer says "剩余额度未知 / allowance not known" for an account it just read.

Deliberately unchanged:

- an **error** reading still knows nothing (ClinePass keeps a balance beside a limits-couldn't-be-read error — the error stands);
- an empty reading with no balance either says nothing, as before;
- the GUI's balance meter rendering is untouched — this is only the routing/knownness side, which is the "at minimum" half of your suggestion.

Verification: `TestBalanceOnlyLiveReadingKnowsTheAccount` drives the live reader through `LoginUsageVia` with your exact reading (provider `minimax-code`, user `MiniMax336627`, `Windows: []`, `Balance: "1740.72 credits"`) and fails "left the account not known" with the change reverted; `TestBalanceOnlyReadingKnowsTheAccount` seeds the persisted reading and reads `lastAllowances` back, same red→green. The Allowances family and the antigravity quota-routing tests pass unchanged; gofmt clean; `go vet ./internal/provider` ok.

